154	     * and separated by spaces (e.g. {@code +61412345678} becomes {@code "+61 412 345 678"}). The
155	     * country code is taken as the longest {@link #KNOWN_COUNTRY_CODES} match, defaulting to a
156	     * two-digit code when none is recognised. It is a derived value; the raw {@code telephone} stays in
157	     * E.164 form.
